       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Having the order settled before the family visits and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for 6,400 mg/day. That dose is twice the maximum, and it adds substantial risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Ibuprofen has a ceiling effect, so the extra drug doesn't give more pain or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia, I can also enter a scheduled acetaminophen order alongside ibuprofen. Or you can ask pharmacy to review the order if you think this patient needs something unusual.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it now."
